messages:
nina (DevEx): FYI during onboarding I hit broken code blocks in the quickstart README. They still show the old JS API and an old env var, so the sample app crashes immediately.
omar (SDK): ugh. which lines? paste please.
nina (DevEx): snippet in README:
```js
const Redwood = require('redwood-js-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
const r = await client.generate('Hello');
console.log(r.text);
```

nina (DevEx): runtime error: `TypeError: client.generate is not a function`. Also the onboarding quickstart uses `REDACTED_API_KEY` placeholder which some folks accidentally left in prod last year.
lee (docs): ahh we missed the v0.9 rename. package is now `@redwood/inference-js` and API split means you must call `client.chat.create` (or `.chat.generate`) and the env var is `RW_API_KEY`.
omar (SDK): SDK default retry went to 0 in v0.9. docs still mention retries: 3. That mismatch explains the transient 429s reported in support. We should recommend explicit retry config in examples.
nina (DevEx): suggested quick fix in README before/after: 
```js
// before (outdated)
const Redwood = require('redwood-js-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
await client.generate('hi');

// after (updated)
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference-js');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY, retry: { maxRetries: 2 } });
const resp = await client.chat.create({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }] });
console.log(resp.choices[0].message.content);
```

lee (docs): good. I'll open a tiny docs PR to fix the snippets, call out env var rename, and add a "migration note" at the top of quickstart. Also will remove any example strings like `REDACTED_API_KEY` and replace with `export RW_API_KEY=your_real_key` + short security note.
omar (SDK): add a small guard in the SDK to detect legacy env var names (`REDWOOD_KEY`, `OLD_API_KEY`) and throw a helpful error suggesting `RW_API_KEY`. I'll open the SDK PR after lunch.
ci-bot: opened examples-smoke workflow for PR branch docs/fix-quickstart -> running.
ci-bot: examples-smoke failed (run 190): caught a placeholder env value in README (good).
lee (docs): added a GH Action check to fail on placeholder values (regex /(REDACTED|PLACEHOLDER|YOUR_KEY)/i). pushed update.
ci-bot: examples-smoke passed (run 191). Node & Python quickstart examples executed against staging fixture.
nina (DevEx): awesome. can we add a note in the onboarding guide to run the examples smoke locally? new hires often miss that step.
omar (SDK): yes, and we'll backport the README fix to release/v0.9.x. thanks for flagging this — tiny copy/paste drift is high impact.
lee (docs): PR merged and backported. closing thread. :white_check_mark:
